\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs22\lang9 Driveway Cost & Material Calculators: Topical Map and ChatGPT Build Pack\par
Prepared 9 October 2026 for a US-facing site. Search figures are Semrush US estimates from your exports and screenshots, written as volume / KD / CPC, with CPC in US dollars. Related keywords overlap, so never add volumes together.\par
1. How to use this doc\par
1. Read Sections 2 to 4 for strategy, architecture and build order.\par
2. Sections 5 and 6 are the topical map. One row is one page and one EAV signature. Keywords in the Fold in column go on that same page, never on new URLs.\par
3. Section 7 lists the data you must source before any page is written.\par
4. Section 8 holds the ChatGPT prompts. Paste 8.1 first, then one build prompt at a time, then 8.7 with one map row per page.\par
5. Section 9 covers launch, links and risks.\par
2. Foundation Brief\par
Source Context. A US-facing set of free driveway cost guides and material calculators. Revenue comes from (1) lead or call network payouts when visitors request contractor quotes, (2) display ads on tool pages, and (3) affiliate commissions on repair and sealing products.\par
Central Entity. Driveway\par
Brand and domain. Driveway Calculators at drivewaycalc.online. Tagline: Driveway cost guides and material calculators. Author: Farrukh Abdullah, researcher and writer. Write the brand in full as Driveway Calculators. It appears in the home page title, the schema, the footer and the lead disclosure text only, so the other title tags stay under 60 characters.\par
Ontology (summary).\par
\f1\bullet  Surfaces: asphalt, concrete (plain and stamped), gravel, pavers, tar and chip, asphalt millings\par
\bullet  Project types: new installation, replacement, resurfacing or overlay, repair, sealcoating\par
\bullet  Cost drivers: area in square feet, thickness in inches, base preparation, removal, labor, delivery, regional price level\par
\bullet  Quantities: tons, cubic yards, square feet, gallons\par
\bullet  Decisions: concrete vs asphalt, resurface vs replace, DIY vs hire\par
\bullet  Supporting materials: gravel, rock, pea gravel, river rock, crusher run, road base (bridge to Driveway through gravel driveways)\par
Central Search Intent. Working out how much a driveway project costs and how much material it needs, so a US homeowner can budget, order materials or request contractor quotes.\par
Buyer personas.\par
1. Homeowner planning a driveway project: highest lead value, arrives on cost and estimator pages.\par
2. DIY builder or small contractor estimating material: arrives on calculators, produces ad revenue and links.\par
3. Landscaper or homeowner buying aggregate: arrives on gravel and rock calculators, produces ad revenue and feeds gravel driveway pages.\par
Core Section. Cost guides, cost estimators and the driveway quantity calculators (asphalt, gravel driveway, concrete driveway). Lead payouts and the highest CPCs (1.76 to 3.83 USD on cost terms) sit here.\par
Outer Section. Aggregate calculators, converters, a material weight reference, repair product guides and a methodology page. They build Historical Data and pass relevance into Core pages as neighborhood content.\par
Topical border (out of scope). Near me, contractor, company and directory queries; city and state pages; the Asphalt 8 video game and other unrelated senses of asphalt; general construction math unrelated to driveways. Concrete and paver calculators (Phase 3) stay scoped to driveways and flat slabs.\par
Balance Law note. Aggregate calculators are Medium relevance to Driveway. Keep their copy on quantity, and add one bridging section per page that links to the matching driveway cost page. Do not let landscaping content spread into the cost pages.\par
Authority sources. Primary: asphaltisbest.com. Its asphalt calculator holds #1 for asphalt calculator and figuring asphalt with roughly 6 to 9 referring domains and 240+ ranking keywords on one URL. Study its single-page tool structure, not its content. Others: pikeindustries.com (calculator with a quote request), concretenetwork.com (754 ranking keywords on one concrete driveway cost page), homewyse.com (estimator-style cost pages), and calculator.net, inchcalculator.com and omnicalculator.com as gravel calculator benchmarks that hold the top three and are not realistic targets.\par
3. Architecture, tech and monetization modules\par
URL rules. Flat, one level, lowercase, hyphenated, trailing slash. No dates and no categories in URLs. Navigation groups: Costs, Calculators, Materials, Repair and Maintenance, About.\par
Page types and templates.\par
\bullet  Cost guide: answer block, range table, cost factors, quick estimate, Q&A\par
\bullet  Cost estimator (tool): inputs, low-to-high result, assumptions, quote CTA\par
\bullet  Quantity calculator (tool): inputs, result, formula, density table\par
\bullet  Converter or reference: input, result, lookup table\par
\bullet  Comparison: side-by-side table, decision rules\par
\bullet  Product guide (affiliate): criteria, picks, how to use\par
\bullet  Hub or pillar: surface comparison, links to every child page\par
Modules on every cost and tool page, in this order.\par
1. Answer block: one declarative sentence with the number or result\par
2. The calculator or quick estimator\par
3. Result block with a Get free quotes CTA (ZIP, project type)\par
4. How it is calculated: formula, default values, editable fields\par
5. Q&A sections, each starting with the direct answer\par
6. Related pages, each link with annotation text stating the relationship\par
7. Sources named in text, last updated date, author\par
8. Disclosure line for leads and affiliate links\par
Recommended stack. Next.js (App Router) with TypeScript, Tailwind and MDX; calculators as pure TypeScript functions with unit tests; static generation. Host on Cloudflare Pages or Vercel Pro (Vercel's free Hobby plan is for non-commercial use, so check current terms). The lead endpoint runs as a Cloudflare Pages Function with D1 storage; on Vercel Pro use a Next.js route handler instead. Analytics: GA4 and Search Console. Reserve ad slot heights to prevent layout shift. Schema: Organization, BreadcrumbList, WebApplication for tools, Article with dateModified. Google limits FAQ rich results to a small set of sites, so keep Q&A visible but do not plan around a rich result.\par
Monetization.\par
\bullet  Leads: build the CTA module now, but switch it on only after a lead or call network approves you and supplies its consent language and routing details (see 8.5).\par
\bullet  Ads: apply to AdSense once 15 to 20 pages are live and check eligibility for your country; move to a premium ad network when its traffic threshold is met (verify current thresholds).\par
\bullet  Affiliate: repair and sealing product guides (Section 6, Seq 31 and 32).\par
Trust. Real author name and bio, a methodology page, sources named in text, a visible last-updated date. Do not invent a US address, reviewer or contractor credential.\par
