- Title tag and meta description come from frontmatter. Fail the build when a title is over 60 characters or a description is over 155.\par
- Internal links: a RelatedLink carries anchor text equal to the destination page title or H1, plus a relationship sentence.\par
- Images: next/image, width and height set, descriptive alt text taken from the map, lazy loading below the fold, WebP or AVIF.\par
- Performance budget on a mid-range phone: LCP under 2.5 s, CLS under 0.1, INP under 200 ms. Fail the CI check if the Lighthouse mobile performance score is under 90 on the home page, one calculator page and one cost guide.\par
- Thank-you pages and API routes are noindex.\par
- A 404 page that links to the hub and the top calculators.\par
- A /methodology/ page template that lists formulas, defaults, source names and retrieval dates from /data/sources.json.\par
8.7 Prompt: write one page\par
Task: write one page as MDX using the map row, the DATA block and the rules in the project instructions.\par
\par
MAP ROW\par
\{\{paste the Table A row and the Table B row for this page\}\}\par
\par
DATA\par
\{\{paste only sourced figures for this page: price ranges with source names and dates, defaults with sources, statistics. A number that is not listed here must not appear.\}\}\par
\par
PAGE TYPE\par
\{\{cost guide, estimator, quantity calculator, comparison, converter, product guide or hub\}\}, using the module order from the page templates.\par
\par
PASS 1: write the page\par
- Open with an AnswerBlock: one declarative sentence containing the page's main number or result.\par
- Cover every Fold in keyword by using its exact words at least once in a natural place on this page: a heading, a sentence, a table row, a list item or an example. Spread them across sections and use the primary keyword in the title, the H1, the first sentence and one H2. Never repeat an exact keyword more than 4 times. If an exact keyword is ungrammatical (for example how much for a asphalt driveway), use a natural close variant and list it in the coverage report. Headings are short questions. Do not create extra pages.\par
- Declare every Micro-context entity from the row in the copy.\par
- State each fact as a plain statement of entity, attribute and value (for example: A 20 by 20 foot driveway is 400 square feet).\par
- Put the answer in the first sentence under every heading and match the grammar of the heading.\par
- Use numerals for counts (4 factors, 5 steps) and list the items straight after the count.\par
- No hedging words, no filler, no marketing adjectives.\par
- Place conditions after the statement.\par
- Bold the answer span in each direct-answer sentence.\par
- Add a worked example whose numbers come from the calculator function (never typed by hand) and a Before you order checklist of 3 to 5 items. Add the internal links from the Contextual bridges column, each with one sentence of annotation text that states the relationship with a verb.\par
- Mark Featured Snippet answers (40 words or fewer) with the comment FS and People Also Ask answers with the comment PAA.\par
- End with a short Disclosure line when the page carries a quote CTA or affiliate links.\par
\par
PASS 2: readability\par
- After the first sentence of each section, vary sentence length, add a one-line transition between sections, and add one worked example per major section using only DATA values or user-entered numbers.\par
- Do not change any first sentence under a heading, any number, any bolded answer, any heading text or any link anchor.\par
\par
PASS 3: audit\par
- Run the checks in 8.8 and print the table. Fix every violation and print the corrected passages.\par
\par
OUTPUT\par
- The final MDX with frontmatter (title, description, slug, type, updated, author, primaryKeyword, keywords, related).\par
- A list of every \{\{DATA\}\} placeholder that still needs a source. A keyword coverage report: a table of each Fold in keyword and the heading or section where it appears.\par
